  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermediate Results Indicator</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="1" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Companies certified under ISO 9001, ISO 22000 and/or HACCP</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2007-01-16" value="6 (baseline may have been overestimated and will n" year="2007">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN"></narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2007-01-16"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2013-03-31"></period-end>
     <target value="+10 additional ones"></target>
     <actual value="12">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">(+6 from original baseline). The economic crisis continues to undermine the interest of companies in quality and ISOcertification.However, at present, a number of companies in the KR sought and obtained international ISO accreditation: 12companies representingvarious sectors (service, manufacturing, food processing) have an international ISO certificate. Of these,three are from the food sector; only two companies so far benefited from the Matching Grant Facility envisioned in the RTBETProject. Nevertheless, there is growing demand among local SMEs &#x2013; especially in the agribusiness sector &#x2013; to seek ISO22000 andHACCP certification due to pressures from destination markets such as Russia and Kazakhstan.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
